%% Figure 3. Evaluation flow from corpus sampling to metric reporting.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Q as 30 OSINT queries<br/>(SecurityOnion / MISP)
    participant SF as sicry_fetch<br/>multi-engine pass
    participant SL as Seed-list filter<br/>(CSAM/weapons exclude)
    participant CAP as Tor-aware capture<br/>(Playwright + SOCKS5)
    participant A1 as Annotator 1
    participant A2 as Annotator 2
    participant ADJ as Adjudicator
    participant MD as Models<br/>(Opus 4.7, GPT-5, UI2Code^N-9B)
    participant R as Reporting

    Q->>SF: queries
    SF->>SL: candidate .onion URLs
    SL->>CAP: 500 filtered URLs
    CAP->>A1: 500 screenshots (blinded, image-only)
    CAP->>A2: 500 screenshots (blinded, image-only)
    A1->>ADJ: per-URL label
    A2->>ADJ: per-URL label
    ADJ->>ADJ: compute Cohen's kappa
    Note over ADJ: gate: kappa >= 0.75<br/>else revise taxonomy
    ADJ->>R: ground-truth labels<br/>(adjudicated)
    CAP->>MD: 500 screenshots
    MD->>R: per-URL label + confidence + note<br/>(per model)
    R->>R: per-class P/R, weighted F1,<br/>confusion matrix, cost/1k URLs
    R->>R: failure analysis<br/>(every conf>=0.9 disagreement)
